NextBSD: link base ICU (libicucore) and describe it with icu-uc.pc.

NextBSD's ICU is one library, libicucore (Apple's swift-foundation-icu,
ICU 76.1) in /usr/lib/system, as on macOS; there are no libicudata,
libicui18n or libicuuc. 2.9.13's CMake build hard-codes those three names
into libxml-2.0.pc's Libs.private and into `xml2-config --libs`, which
would break every consumer.

libxml-2.0.pc now carries ICU as `Requires.private: icu-uc` (upstream
does the same with icu-i18n from 2.10), and xml2-config, which has no
pkg-config, prints -L/usr/lib/system -licucore. The link itself goes
through CMake's FindICU, whose cache variables build-userland.sh points
at libicucore.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -463,7 +463,10 @@
 	if(WIN32)
 		set(ICU_LIBS "-licudt -licuin -licuuc")
 	else()
-		set(ICU_LIBS "-licudata -licui18n -licuuc")
+		# NextBSD: base ICU is the one library libicucore in /usr/lib/system,
+		# which icu-uc.pc describes; there is no libicudata/libicui18n/libicuuc.
+		set(ICU_LIBS "-L/usr/lib/system -licucore")
+		set(ICU_PC_REQUIRES "icu-uc")
 	endif()
 endif()
 
--- a/libxml-2.0.pc.in
+++ b/libxml-2.0.pc.in
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 Version: @VERSION@
 Description: libXML library version2.
 Requires:
+Requires.private: @ICU_PC_REQUIRES@
 Libs: -L${libdir} -lxml2
-Libs.private: @ICU_LIBS@ @THREAD_LIBS@ @Z_LIBS@ @LZMA_LIBS@ @ICONV_LIBS@ @M_LIBS@ @WIN32_EXTRA_LIBADD@ @LIBS@
+Libs.private: @THREAD_LIBS@ @Z_LIBS@ @LZMA_LIBS@ @ICONV_LIBS@ @M_LIBS@ @WIN32_EXTRA_LIBADD@ @LIBS@
 Cflags: @XML_INCLUDEDIR@ @XML_CFLAGS@
